        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: The Liberator Magazine, Video Watchdog\n- People: Brian Kasoro, Gayle Smaller, Tazz Hunter, Kenya McKnight, Marcus Harcus, Mike Clark, Tim Lucas, Donna Lucas\n- Places: Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA\n- Topics: magazine publishing\n\nFacts:\n- Video Watchdog was a bimonthly, digest-size film magazine that was published from 1990 to 2017.\n- Video Watchdog was published by Tim Lucas, who served as publisher and editor, and Donna Lucas, who served as art director and co-publisher.\n- The Liberator Magazine is a publication and production company based in Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA.\n- The Liberator Magazine was started by Brian Kasoro, Gayle Smaller, Tazz Hunter, Kenya McKnight, Marcus Harcus, and Mike Clark.\n- The Liberator Magazine published its first release on July 21, 2002.",
